<title>USA: Nationwide Finl unit sells $100 capital secs.</title>
<headline>Nationwide Finl unit sells $100 capital secs.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following issue of capital securities from Nationwide Financial Services Inc's Nationwide Financial Services Capital Trust was priced on Thursday, according to co-lead manager Credit Suisse First Boston.</p>
<p>Morgan Stanley &amp; Co was also co-lead manager.</p>
<p>BORROWER NATIONWIDE FINANCIAL SERVICES CAPITAL TRUST</p>
<p>AMT $100 MLN	 COUPON 7.899 PCT  MATURITY 3/01/2037</p>
<p>TYPE CAP SECS	ISS PRICE 100.00  FIRST PAY DATE 9/01/97</p>
<p>LAST MOODY'S A1    SPREAD 102 BP     PAY FREQ SEMI-ANNUAL</p>
<p>LAST S&amp;P SINGLE-A			  CALLABLE MAKE-WHOLE</p>
<p>							    AT TREAS +20 BP</p>
<p>NOTE: Includes contingency tax call language.</p>
<p>((U.S. corporate bond unit, 212 859-1672))</p>
